    "raw_content": "Regarded as one of Louis Auchincloss's most accomplished 
novels, THE RECTOR OF JUSTIN centers on Frank Prescott, the founder of an 
exclusive school for boys in New England. As his story is told through the eyes 
of those drawn into his charismatic orbit, Prescott's character—at once admirable
and enigmatic—is gradually revealed. There is Brian Aspinwall, a young teacher 
and the rector's latest protégé; Horace Havistock, Prescott's oldest friend, who 
is now a conspicuous failure; Francis's daughter, who concludes that her father 
has always loved the school more than his family; and finally, a wealthy trustee 
who understands that Prescott is as much the product of the school as its 
creator. THE RECTOR OF JUSTIN is told with wit and elegance; it is a wise and 
resonant work, widely recognized as Auchincloss's masterpiece.\n\n[Text as 
displayed on Amazon product page; Goodreads description for the same ISBN closely
parallels this wording.]",
