{"query": {"id": "20260623024025547485_a4cbce99", "handle": "q3", "text": "\"The 
Rector of Justin\" 1964 review \"New York Times\"", "importance": "core"}, 
"items": [{"id": "20260623024240129064_7e71bd84", "type": "Claim", "text": "In 
his 1964 New York Times review, Granville Hicks describes \"The Rector of 
Justin\" as a serious and ambitious novel about an elite boys’ boarding school 
and its aging headmaster.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], 
"citations": [8]}, {"id": "20260623024240823515_0c09984d", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "The New York Times review portrays the boarding school in \"The Rector 
of Justin\" as a microcosm of the American upper-class establishment and 
emphasizes the rector’s charisma, authority, and moral conflicts.", "source_ids":
["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], "citations": [8]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241211581_8ec14682", "type": "Claim", "text": "Granville Hicks 
praises Louis Auchincloss’s control of multiple narrators in \"The Rector of 
Justin,\" arguing that this structure deepens the novel’s psychological portrait 
of the headmaster.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], 
"citations": [8]}, {"id": "20260623024241236901_5015d778", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "The 1964 New York Times review interprets \"The Rector of Justin\" as a 
nuanced critique of privileged educational institutions and their moral 
compromises rather than as a simple attack on the upper class.", "source_ids": 
["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], "citations": [8]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241264095_9cc8b711", "type": "Claim", "text": "According to the 1964 
New York Times review, the chief strengths of \"The Rector of Justin\" lie in its
subtle characterization and detailed depiction of social milieu, not in plot 
surprises.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], "citations": [8]}, 
{"id": "20260623024241288345_acbaf5d0", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 1979 New 
York Times essay \"In Praise of Louis Auchincloss\" identifies \"The Rector of 
Justin\" as one of Auchincloss’s major or defining novels.", "source_ids": 
["20260623024239693087_6e1a88ad"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241313143_7270a7be", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 1979 New York 
Times essay characterizes \"The Rector of Justin\" as both a popular and 
critically successful novel within Louis Auchincloss’s body of work.", 
"source_ids": ["20260623024239693087_6e1a88ad"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241334164_08214e75", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 1979 New York 
Times essay presents \"The Rector of Justin\" as a high point in Auchincloss’s 
exploration of upper‑class institutions and moral responsibility.", "source_ids":
["20260623024239693087_6e1a88ad"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241356943_f15c7ec5", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 1979 New York 
Times essay suggests that \"The Rector of Justin\" exhibits greater thematic 
depth and psychological insight than some of Auchincloss’s other novels.", 
"source_ids": ["20260623024239693087_6e1a88ad"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241376081_db7da1f3", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 1964 New York 
Times article \"A Sorting Out\" reports that \"The Rector of Justin\" was a best 
seller and a serious contender in that year’s major fiction awards.", 
"source_ids": ["20260623024239712986_d773ad89"], "citations": [10]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241397172_e5b632d0", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 1964 New York 
Times article \"A Sorting Out\" describes \"The Rector of Justin\" as an 
accomplished, traditional realist or society novel about the American upper 
class.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239712986_d773ad89"], "citations": [10]}, 
{"id": "20260623024241416612_8c40fe75", "type": "Claim", "text": "By contrasting 
\"The Rector of Justin\" with Saul Bellow’s \"Herzog,\" the 1964 New York Times 
article implies that Auchincloss’s novel was widely respected but stylistically 
more conventional than its award‑winning rival.", "source_ids": 
["20260623024239712986_d773ad89"], "citations": [10]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241439206_b038106c", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The review \"A 
Crucible Covered With Ivy\" in The New York Times (1964) is described as treating
Louis Auchincloss’s \"The Rector of Justin\" as a serious, literate exploration 
focused on the character and moral compromises of an aging headmaster of an elite
boys’ boarding school.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], 
"citations": [8]}, {"id": "20260623024241470162_8045f94a", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The 1964 review notes that the school in \"The Rector of Justin\" is 
presented as a microcosm for the American upper‑class establishment and comments 
on Auchincloss’s portrayal of the rector’s charisma, authority, and inner 
conflicts.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], "citations": [8]}, 
{"id": "20260623024241496697_f31ab2e4", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Granville 
Hicks’s review emphasizes Auchincloss’s skill in portraying the rector through 
multiple viewpoints and praises his control of the novel’s multiple‑narrator 
structure.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], "citations": [8]}, 
{"id": "20260623024241522232_7b4014e8", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 1964 New
York Times review interprets \"The Rector of Justin\" as a critique, though not a
simplistic one, of upper‑class educational institutions and their moral 
compromises.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], "citations": 
[8]}, {"id": "20260623024241551783_9f58a1c5", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 
review states that the novel’s strength lies in its subtle, closely observed 
treatment of character and social milieu rather than in plot surprises.", 
"source_ids": ["20260623024239665361_f1de7223"], "citations": [8]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241577182_1c8e87c6", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 1979 New York 
Times essay on Louis Auchincloss is summarized as singling out \"The Rector of 
Justin\" as a particularly significant and successful novel, calling it one of 
his major or defining works.", "source_ids": ["20260623024239693087_6e1a88ad"], 
"citations": [9]}, {"id": "20260623024241602860_e5beb58e", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The same 1979 essay highlights \"The Rector of Justin\" for both its 
popular and critical success within Auchincloss’s career.", "source_ids": 
["20260623024239693087_6e1a88ad"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260623024241631112_d20f850a", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 1979 
